{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghQeMfQovgeNHdgiTSjh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Vanadate contains V(V), which is d⁰. It has no d electrons, so it has no d–d transitions. The bands at 37 210, 44 860 and 52 370 cm⁻¹ have ε of about 3 000 to 10 000 M⁻¹ cm⁻¹. That is typical of ligand-to-metal charge transfer (O→V) in a tetrahedral oxo-anion, where the transitions are Laporte-allowed and intense.\n\nThe bands correspond to the LMCT transitions 1t1 → 2e and 1t1 → 2t2, with spin-orbit and multiplet splitting. They are not crystal-field transitions.\n\nThe ligand-field model cannot give Dq or B from these bands, for three reasons:\n- A d⁰ ion has no Racah electron-repulsion parameters to fit, because there are no d–d terms. The Tanabe–Sugano d² to d⁸ treatment does not apply.\n- Fitting the LMCT energies to a Tanabe–Sugano diagram would give meaningless numbers.\n- The 2e–2t2 gap in an oxo-anion is related to the tetrahedral splitting Δt. However, the observed bands are charge-transfer energies, so they do not give Δt directly. The band spacing of about 7 500 cm⁻¹ and about 7 600 cm⁻¹ is not a ligand-field splitting either.\n\nI am therefore giving no values for Dq or B.\n\n{\"Dq\": null, \"B\": null, \"C\": null, \"out_of_scope\": true, \"reason\": \"VO4^3- is d0 (V5+), so the intense bands are O→V charge-transfer transitions and no d-d ligand-field fit for Dq or B is possible.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":253,"cache_read_input_tokens":7806,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":253,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff831392-7c99-4e02-83f1-acb4a2b1b1b8","uuid":"a0ceff65-88e3-4fe